# Go: the canonical generated module (root go.mod + recursive .go) IS tracked as a reviewed derived
# artifact (verified byte-exact against the pristine Buildx layer by the pre-commit staged-index check), so
# *.go is NOT ignored.  Ignore ONLY this repository's transient local control/crash residue: the exact root
# .fido/ control dir and any abandoned reserved sibling temps.  A NESTED .fido is an emission ERROR and is
# deliberately NOT ignored (it must stay visible if it ever appears).
/.fido/
**/*.fido-tmp-v1
/fido
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# Plugin / sink build artifacts (generated in the build, never tracked).
/sink_test
*.cmi
*.cmo
*.cmx
*.cmxs
*.o

# Python: the gates under tools/ are SOURCE (*.py, tracked and reviewed).  Interpreter-derived bytecode is
# CPython-version-specific, goes stale against its own .py source, and must never be a live tool authority.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Environment
.env

# Rocq build artifacts — .v sources are checked in, these are not
*.glob
*.vo
*.vok
*.vos
*.vio
*.aux
.*.aux
.lia.cache
.nia.cache
.coq-native/
_build/

# Assistant tool residue.  The repository owns this exclusion deliberately, so the working-tree inventory
# `make check` archives is determined by the repository alone and two clones of one commit archive the
# same tree.
/.claude/

# Lean 4 POC build products (lean/README.md); never tracked, never a build input
/lean/.lake/
